rage; the Couchbase SDK’s requestTracer environment wiring is optional. [Upstream unit test](https://github.com/couchbase/couchbase-jvm-clients/blob/3.11.3/tracing-micrometer-observation/src/integrationTest/java/com/couchbase/client/tracing/observation/ObservationRequestTracerTests.java)\",\nstats/com.couchbase.client/tracing-micrometer-observation/3.11.3/execution-metrics.json:63:        \"A full end-to-end Couchbase request test would additionally require java-client/test infrastructure and a running Couchbase cluster; local Gradle and Native Image verification remain authoritative.\",\nstats/com.couchbase.client/metrics-micrometer/3.11.3/execution-metrics.json:48:      \"agent_guidance\": \"Use MicrometerMeter.wrap(new SimpleMeterRegistry()) and exercise counters, value recorders, and tag handling. Keep coverage independent of a live Couchbase cluster or Prometheus exporter.\",\nstats/com.couchbase.client/metrics-micrometer/3.11.3/execution-metrics.json:50:        \"Live Cluster integration would require separate Couchbase infrastructure, but is unnecessary for meaningful adapter coverage.\"\nmetadata/com.couchbase.client/tracing-micrometer-observation/index.json:9:    \"description\" : \"This library integrates the Couchbase JVM SDK with Micrometer Observation by translating Couchbase request lifecycle events into Micrometer observations. It enables applications to collect and export Couchbase tracing and observation data through Micrometer-compatible handlers.\",\nmetadata/com.couchbase.client/metrics-micrometer/index.json:9:    \"description\" : \"Couchbase Metrics Micrometer integrates the Couchbase JVM client’s metrics API with Micrometer’s MeterRegistry. It adapts Couchbase counters and value recorders to Micrometer instruments so applications can export Couchbase client metrics through Micrometer-compatible monitoring systems.\",\ntests/src/org.springframework.boot/spring-boot-data-couchbase-test/4.1.1/settings.gradle:20:rootProject.name = 'org.springframe